{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#259","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#259","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#259\",\"parent_revision\":\"d5b9b7584939f50b32a27b6578a1977bf718bc0e\",\"root_revision\":\"2da9233fcc089f0f90da356defd91670f0ee85fe52b02de0cb6a9d5c8ac6903e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWrap `file_metrics.py` (count/scan commands with `--json` support) as MCP tools. Provides structured document analysis for the rewriting workflow router. Tools: `count_document_metrics`, `scan_documents`, `compare_versions`.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `file_metrics.py` accessible to the-rewrite-room (shared or copied) | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/the-rewrite-room/scripts/` or reference to summarizer's copy |\\n| 2 | `--json` output flag available in `file_metrics.py` | DERIVABLE | Inspect script interface |\\n| 3 | the-rewrite-room plugin can add MCP infrastructure | DERIVABLE | Check `plugins/the-rewrite-room/` structure |\\n| 4 | `compare_versions` capability: does file_metrics.py support it or must it be custom? | DERIVABLE | Inspect script; if absent, implement as new tool using `difflib` |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information derivable from codebase inspection.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **the-rewrite-room: document analysis mcp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: MCP backlog audit 2026-02-23\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested Location\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/the-rewrite-room/mcp/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Docs. Additive only. Low risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- MCP tool `count_document_metrics` accepts a file path, returns token count and structural metrics\\n- MCP tool `scan_documents` accepts a directory, returns per-file metrics for the rewriting workflow\\n- MCP tool `compare_versions` accepts two file paths, returns a diff summary indicating what changed between versions\\n- All tools registered in `plugins/the-rewrite-room/.mcp.json`\\n- FastMCP server validated with `uv run fastmcp list`\\n- Tools appear when the the-rewrite-room plugin is installed\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/scripts/file_metrics.py` \u2014 script to wrap (or shared from summarizer)\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/scripts/run_mcp_server.py` \u2014 new MCP server (PEP 723, FastMCP)\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/.mcp.json` \u2014 MCP server registration\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bump\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent using the the-rewrite-room plugin, I need `file_metrics.py` exposed as MCP tools so I can request structured document metrics to drive the rewriting workflow router without shell access.\\n\",\"digest\":\"333d3f550d4458ef156f8a1d1a748c5770e4196b0d31c6efe9063721de0db59a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg1tOw\"}"}